# Unity 6 C# language subset

Unity **6000.x** compiles with **C# 9.0** (Roslyn), not the latest .NET SDK. The runtime is **not** .NET 5+ — types like `IsExternalInit` are missing unless you add a polyfill per assembly.

**Authority:** [C# compiler and language version (Unity 6)](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.4/Documentation/Manual/csharp-compiler.html)

## Never use `init` accessors

**Do not** generate `{ get; init; }` in `Assets/Scripts` or `Assets/Tests`. Unity fails compile with:

`CS0518: Predefined type 'System.Runtime.CompilerServices.IsExternalInit' is not defined or imported`

Use `{ get; set; }`, a constructor, or a static factory instead — even for “immutable” DTOs and object-initializer presets.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — breaks Unity compile
public bool ShowCombatAction { get; init; }

// ✅ GOOD — matches shipped patterns (e.g. ItemListPickerLayout)
public bool ShowCombatAction { get; set; }
```

Do **not** add `IsExternalInit` polyfills to work around this unless the team explicitly approves (default: avoid).

## Do not use (unsupported or breaks asmdefs)

| Feature | Why | Use instead |
|---------|-----|-------------|
| `init` accessors | CS0518 — see above | `set`, constructor, or factory |
| `record` / `record struct` | Needs `IsExternalInit`; poor fit for Unity serialization | `sealed class` / `struct` DTOs |
| `required` members | Newer C# / runtime gaps | Constructor validation, `[SerializeField]` + defaults |
| File-scoped namespaces | Not in Unity’s supported subset | Block `namespace { }` |
| Module initializers, covariant returns, etc. | [Listed unsupported](https://docs.unity3d.com/6000.4/Documentation/Manual/csharp-compiler.html) | Supported alternatives only |

## Prefer for DTOs and results

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — init / record
public sealed record ProtocolResolveResult
{
    public IReadOnlyList<CombatActionResult> TargetResults { get; init; }
}

// ✅ GOOD — classic property + object initializer
public sealed class ProtocolResolveResult
{
    public IReadOnlyList<CombatActionResult> TargetResults { get; set; } =
        Array.Empty<CombatActionResult>();
}
```

## Nullable, async, pattern matching

- **Nullable reference types** — OK; project enables `-nullable:enable` in `Assets/csc.rsp`.
- **Async/await** — OK where Unity APIs allow; don’t assume full .NET BCL on all targets.
- **Pattern matching, switch expressions, `readonly struct`** — OK when they compile under C# 9.

## Custom asmdefs (`GridDungeon.Core`, tests)

Separate assemblies do **not** inherit Unity’s default polyfills. If code must use `init`/`record` (discouraged), add **one** internal polyfill **per asmdef**:

```csharp
namespace System.Runtime.CompilerServices
{
    internal static class IsExternalInit { }
}
```

Default team choice: **avoid** `init`/`record` rather than maintaining polyfills.

## Do not “upgrade” language version casually

- Do **not** set `-langVersion:10` (or higher) in `csc.rsp` without team agreement and full recompile/IL2CPP smoke tests.
- Changing **API Compatibility Level** is a separate, higher-risk migration — it does not make `init` officially supported.

## Agent / codegen

When generating C# under `Assets/Scripts` or `Assets/Tests`, use this subset. Complements `unity-csharp-naming`, `unity-csharp-formatting`, `unity-clean-code-principles`.
